```
Hmm wait — the label shows the target mode. In day mode: "Night Mode · 夜晚模式" with a moon icon. In night mode: "Day Mode · 白天模式" with a sun icon. JS updates the label. But the label has t-en/t-zh spans — when the language mode is en-only/zh-only, the other one gets hidden. Good, it's consistent.

But the JS needs to swap the label text. Structure: put a data attribute on the label span? Easier: JS sets innerHTML:
- Target night: `<span class="t-en">Night Mode</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="t-zh" lang="zh">夜晚模式</span>`
- Target day: `<span class="t-en">Day Mode</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="t-zh" lang="zh">白天模式</span>`
This works with the existing language mode CSS (the .t-en/.t-zh/.sep classes are globally styled).

CSS:
```css
  .theme-btn{
    display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:9px;
    font:inherit; font-size:.92rem; font-weight:600; cursor:pointer;
    color:var(--ink); background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line);
    padding:8px 16px; border-radius:999px;
    transition:background-color .6s ease, color .6s ease, border-color .6s ease, box-shadow .3s ease;
  }
  .theme-btn:hover{ box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(21,101,192,.2); }
  .theme-icon{
    position:relative; width:15px; height:15px; border-radius:50%;
    transition:background .5s ease, box-shadow .5s ease;
  }
  /* in day mode, the button offers "Night" → show the moon */
  body:not(.night) .theme-icon{
    background:radial-gradient(circle at 68% 32%, transparent 0 54%, #dfe6f3 55%);
  }
  /* in night mode, the button offers "Day" → show the sun */
  body.night .theme-icon{
    background:#ffca28;
    box-shadow:0 0 8px rgba(255,202,40,.85);
  }
```
Wait, the crescent moon: `radial-gradient(circle at 68% 32%, transparent 0 54%, #dfe6f3 55%)` — the center of the gradient is at (68%,32%); within a radius of 54% of the smaller dimension it's transparent, then colored beyond that. The resulting shape = a disk with a transparent circular bite taken out of the top-right → a crescent in the bottom-left. The crescent color #dfe6f3 (light) — visible on the button's background (day: white card → a light gray crescent, low contrast!). On a white background a #dfe6f3 crescent is nearly invisible. For day mode use a darker crescent color: #8fa8c8 or #64b5f6 (sky-300). On a white background #64b5f6 is visible. In night mode the icon is a sun anyway. So the day-mode crescent: use `#5b8ec9`. Let's use #5b8ec9.

Hmm, but the "transparent" part lets the button background (white) show through — good.

Also `.controls-right{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; }`

And the controls hint text: add "Theme:"? The hint is currently "View:". The theme button is separate and self-evident with the icon + label. Fine.

**Edit 9: JS theme toggle** (after the language toggle block):
```js
  // ---- Theme toggle (Day / Night) ----
  var themeBtn = document.getElementById('themeBtn');
  var themeLabel = themeBtn.querySelector('.theme-label');
  var LABEL_NIGHT = '<span class="t-en">Night Mode</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="t-zh" lang="zh">夜晚模式</span>';
  var LABEL_DAY   = '<span class="t-en">Day Mode</span><span class="sep">·</span><span class="t-zh" lang="zh">白天模式</span>';
  function applyTheme(theme, persist){
    var night = (theme === 'night');
    document.body.classList.toggle('night', night);
    themeLabel.innerHTML = night ? LABEL_DAY : LABEL_NIGHT;
    themeBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', night ? 'Switch to day mode · 切换到白天模式' : 'Switch to night mode · 切换到夜晚模式');
    if(persist){
      try{ localStorage.setItem('sky-theme', theme); }catch(err){}
    }
  }
  themeBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){
    applyTheme(document.body.classList.contains('night') ? 'day' : 'night', true);
  });
  var savedTheme = null;
  try{ savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('sky-theme'); }catch(err){}
  if(savedTheme === 'night' || savedTheme === 'day'){ applyTheme(savedTheme, false); }
```
To avoid a flash on load, apply the saved theme early — the script is at the end of body, so there might be a brief flash of the day theme before it switches to night. Acceptable (the .7s transition covers it). To be cleaner, we could put a tiny inline script in the head before the CSS that sets the class. That's a nice trick:
```html
<script>
  try{ if(localStorage.getItem('sky-theme') === 'night') document.documentElement.classList.add('night-early'); }catch(e){}
</script>
```
Hmm, but the class needs to be on body... the body doesn't exist yet in the head. Add the class to <html> and use a `:root.night`-style CSS? My CSS selectors use `body.night`. I could support both: `body.night, html.night body`? That's cumbersome. The simplest: the end-of-body script sets it immediately — the flash risk is minimal (the script runs during parsing, before the first paint, since it's a synchronous script at the end of body). Actually, a synchronous inline script at the end of body usually executes before the first paint. Good enough.

**Edit 10: reduced motion** (at the end of the CSS):
```css
