Change the nav's aria-label from "Language selection" to "Page controls".

Now, the shared theme transition rule — where to place it? After the "Language modes" section, before the Footer. Elements: body, .card (redundant with the .js .card update, but needed for no-JS), .card-head, .col, .col-label, .equation, .controls, .lang-toggle, footer, footer code, .theme-btn (has its own, skip), .level-badge? (no change). h3.subhead's color variable change — add h3.subhead? It uses var(--sky-900); the color transition — add `.card-head h2, h3.subhead` to the list for smoothness. And `.col strong` inherits the body's color — the inherited color transitions on the parent? The inherited color doesn't animate per element... actually, `color` transitions on the element where it's set (body). Children that inherit get the new value instantly? No — inherited properties: when body's color transitions, the computed inherited value changes over time, and the children that inherit follow smoothly (the transition applies on the body; the children's computed color = the inherited animated value). Yes, children inherit the animated value frame-by-frame. Good — no need to add p/li.

But `strong`'s font-weight is the same, and the color is inherited → smooth. `code`'s chip: explicit background + color → included. `.col-label` is explicit → included. `.equation` is explicit background → included. `.equation`'s text inherits from .col → smooth. `.math` inherits. `.frac .num`'s border is currentColor → border-color uses currentColor... a border-bottom with currentColor — it follows the animated color, but the border-color property itself doesn't transition... currentColor updates continuously as the color animates (because the inherited color animates frame-by-frame, currentColor tracks it). Good.

`.sep`'s color variable → inherits? .sep has an explicit color var(--sky-300) — add to the list? It's a small separator dot; instant change is OK, but let's include the h2 .sep. Let's add a reasonably complete list:

