Also `#topBtn`'s color:#fff stays the same. OK.

Also the `.hero` box-shadow variable change (the shadow variable differs in night) — .hero has box-shadow:var(--shadow) — no transition on .hero; the shadow changes instantly. Add .hero to the transition list (the box-shadow part). The .hero's background is now transparent (the layer handles it) → no background transition needed. Add `.hero{ transition:box-shadow .6s ease; }`? .hero has no own transition rule; add it to the shared list.

Now, the z-index of the `.hero-sky` layers: .hero-night z-index:0, .hero-day z-index:1, .sun z-index:2, .hero-inner position:relative z-index:3. The original .hero-inner was position:relative (no z-index) — the sun was previously auto-stacked... originally: .hero (position relative), .sun absolute, .hero-inner relative → the sun is before hero-inner in the DOM and both are positioned → hero-inner is painted on top of the sun? They don't spatially overlap much (the sun is in the top-right). Now with explicit z-index it's safe.

Also the `.hero`'s overflow hidden + border-radius — the layers inherit the clipping. Good.

The `.sky-day`'s transition: opacity .7s ease — plus the initial `opacity:1` is implicit.

